This dossier supports first-time, never-licensed applicants preparing for the regular passenger-car written knowledge and road sign tests in Michigan. The issuing authority is the Michigan Department of State, led by the Secretary of State, and the source is the handbook What Every Driver Must Know. This section covers children left unattended in vehicles, air bag safety, the Basic Speed Law and standard Michigan speed limits, construction zones with their speed limits, fines and points, merging in work zones, green-light maintenance vehicles, yielding to and moving over for emergency vehicles, and stopping for school buses. The handbook pages do not state an official question count, passing score, test format or time limit for the Secretary of State knowledge test, so this dossier asserts no value for any of them and records each as an explicit unknown. Practice scoring follows only the accepted LearningLoop product policy, never an official threshold.
